## HTML

The plain HTML way is to put it in a `&lt;form&gt;` wherein you specify the desired target URL in the `action` attribute.

```xml
&lt;form action=&quot;https://google.com&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Go to Google&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
```

If necessary, set CSS `display: inline;` on the form to keep it in the flow with the surrounding text. Instead of `&lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;` in above example, you can also use `&lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;`. The only difference is that the `&lt;button&gt;` element allows children.

You&#39;d intuitively expect to be able to use `&lt;button href=&quot;https://google.com&quot;&gt;` analogous with the `&lt;a&gt;` element, but unfortunately no, this attribute does not exist according to [HTML specification][1].

## CSS

If CSS is allowed, simply use an `&lt;a&gt;` which you style to look like a button.

```xml
&lt;a href=&quot;https://google.com&quot; class=&quot;button&quot;&gt;Go to Google&lt;/a&gt;
```

```css
a.button {
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border: 1px outset buttonborder;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: buttontext;
    background-color: buttonface;
    text-decoration: none;
}
```

Or pick one of those many CSS libraries like [Bootstrap][2].

```xml
&lt;a href=&quot;https://google.com&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;&gt;Go to Google&lt;/a&gt;
```

Noted should be that, historically, the CSS [`appearance:button`][3] property worked as well in some browsers, but this was experimental and ended up being considered a misfeature. Only `none` or `auto` are allowed on `&lt;a&gt;` elements.

## JavaScript

If JavaScript is allowed, set the `window.location.href`.

```xml
&lt;input type=&quot;button&quot; onclick=&quot;location.href=&#39;https://google.com&#39;;&quot; value=&quot;Go to Google&quot; /&gt;
```

Instead of `&lt;input type=&quot;button&quot;&gt;` in above example, you can also use `&lt;button&gt;`. The only difference is that the `&lt;button&gt;` element allows children.


  [1]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-button-element
  [2]: https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/components/buttons/
  [3]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/appearance
